[node name="TelegraphController" type="Node3D" parent="."]
script = ExtResource("3_tgctl")
attack_profile = ExtResource("4_tpatk")
block_profile = ExtResource("5_tpblk")
roll_profile = ExtResource("6_tprol")
charge_red_profile = ExtResource("17_tpcred")
charge_blue_profile = ExtResource("18_tpcblu")
charge_green_profile = ExtResource("19_tpcgrn")
editor_description = "D7 cues layer (story 1-10, extended 5-3). READ-ONLY consumer of the queued state signals, wired by the runner through the connect seams - signal payloads only, never a state handle, never a mutator call. AudioStreamPlayer children route to the CombatCues bus; telegraph shapes/spark/flash are in-scene primitives (FacingMarker precedent - no import pipeline for meshes). Shapes are root-relative markers ON PURPOSE: nothing here yaws, so the 1-7b single-yaw-source contract holds (no second atan2). NO _physics_process (F1). HEIGHTS, re-seated in 3-0b Pass 3b: these were authored in 1-10 against the BOX (cone/shield 0.5 above the box top at root +1.0, disc 0.05 above the box floor at root -1.0), when the hero was box-only and no model existed. 3-0a's paladin then landed feet-at-root-0, floating a full 1.0 above the box floor, which hid the mismatch. Pass 3b drops the model to the box floor and drops AttackCone/BlockShield/DeflectSpark by the same 1.0 so they stay with the body: they now read at BODY HEIGHT on the model (root +0.5 / +0.3) rather than overhead. RollDisc and HitFlash are unchanged — both key off the box, which was already correctly grounded. Accepted cost, ruled by the operator at Pass 3b: cone/shield now intersect the model's head and shoulders and are partly occluded by it. Pinned by test/integration/test_vertical_alignment.gd. STORY 5-3 (AC 10) adds a SINGLE shared ChargeMarker shape (Shapes/ChargeMarker, an orb) and THREE colour-keyed profiles (charge_red/blue/green) — unlike attack/block/roll, the charge profile's colour is applied to the shared shape's material AT DISPATCH TIME (on_action_state_changed), not pre-baked in _ready(), since one physical node stands in for three colours rather than one shape per profile. Also adds CueCastSuccess (S5, AC 13) played on the EXISTING, previously-unwired card_cast_resolved signal — a one-shot success cue, distinct from the ongoing CHARGING sting."

